      "blockId": "tour:lead:e3456bc1f4d270f4",
      "field": "lead",
      "sourceTextSha256": "55691566ba2704eabefe64b2f6df12cc2d5be88e81252fe1f0414cb718d0e366",
      "text": "Over 17 days, you’ll travel through several very different regions of Brazil. Start in Rio de Janeiro, with its oceanfront, Corcovado, Sugarloaf Mountain and the Tijuca Forest. Then continue to Ilha Grande, Iguaçu Falls, the wetlands of the Pantanal, and the clear rivers and caves of Bonito. Finish in north-eastern Brazil, among the colonial streets of São Luís and the white dunes of Lençóis Maranhenses.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw63kpsu-m686b5-amanda",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Word document supplies a route list and separate day descriptions but has no equivalent introductory overview combining these sights."
      }
    },
